  MOD_HTTP3 INSTALLATION OVERVIEW

  Quick Start
  -----------

  For complete build and configuration documentation, see CONFIGURATION.md.
  For httpd runtime directives and VirtualHost setup, see CONFIGURATION_HTTPD.md.

     $ git clone https://github.com/machine-moon/mod_http3.git
     $ cd mod_http3
     $ git submodule sync --recursive
     $ git submodule update --init --recursive
     $ cmake -B build
     $ cmake --build build -j$(nproc)
     $ cmake --build build -j$(nproc) --target tests

  The first build downloads nothing -- all dependencies are compiled from
  the git submodules already present in the repository (OpenSSL, APR,
  APR-util, httpd, nghttp3, googletest).  This takes several minutes.
  Subsequent builds reuse the cached result and are fast.

  Build outputs:

     build/lib/mod_http3.so        Apache DSO
     build/bin/mod_http3_tests     Google Test binary

  To install to a prefix (e.g. /opt/mod_http3):

     $ cmake --install build --prefix /opt/mod_http3


  Submodules
  ----------

  Submodules must be initialized before the first build:

     $ git submodule sync --recursive
     $ git submodule update --init --recursive

  To reset submodules to a known-clean state (discards local changes):

     $ git submodule foreach --recursive 'git reset --hard || :'
     $ git submodule foreach --recursive 'git clean -ffdx || :'


  Overriding Build Variables
  --------------------------

  Variables are passed to cmake with the -Dflag at configure time:

     $ cmake -B build -DVARIABLE=VALUE

  Multiple -Dflags may be combined:

     $ cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug -DENABLE_ASAN=ON

  CMake caches variable values after the first configure run.  Pass
  a variable again to change its value on a subsequent configure.

  Boolean options accept any of the following values (case-insensitive):

     True  values: ON  YES  TRUE  1  Y
     False values: OFF NO   FALSE 0  N  IGNORE  NOTFOUND

  Reference: https://cmake.org/cmake/help/latest/command/if.html#constant


  Build Options
  -------------

  CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE        (default: Release)
      Controls compiler optimization and debug symbol generation.
      Accepted values: Debug, Release.

      $ cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug

  BUILD_MODULE            (default: ON)
      Build mod_http3.so, the Apache DSO.  Disable to build only tests
      or examples without the module itself.

      $ cmake -B build -DBUILD_MODULE=OFF

  BUILD_EXAMPLES          (default: ON)
      Build standalone example programs (server, quic_client_test, etc.).

      $ cmake -B build -DBUILD_EXAMPLES=OFF

  BUILD_TESTS             (default: ON)
      Build the Google Test suite.

      $ cmake -B build -DBUILD_TESTS=OFF

  ENABLE_ASAN             (default: OFF)
      Enable Address Sanitizer.  Requires CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug.
      The build will fail if ASAN is enabled with a non-Debug build type.

      $ cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug -DENABLE_ASAN=ON

  ENABLE_UBSAN            (default: OFF)
      Enable Undefined Behavior Sanitizer.  Requires CMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug.

      $ cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug -DENABLE_UBSAN=ON

  ENABLE_WERROR           (default: OFF)
      Treat all compiler warnings as errors (-Werror).

      $ cmake -B build -DENABLE_WERROR=ON

  VENDOR_SYSTEM           (default: ON)
      ON  -- build OpenSSL, APR, APR-util, and httpd from submodules.
             This is the default and requires no system packages beyond
             a C compiler, CMake, and Ninja.
      OFF -- find dependencies on PATH using find_package / config scripts.
             Requires apxs, apr-1-config, apu-1-config, and OpenSSL >= 3.5.0
             to be on PATH.

      $ cmake -B build -DVENDOR_SYSTEM=OFF

  DEPENDENCIES_PARALLEL   (default: 6)
      Number of parallel jobs used when building vendored dependencies
      (OpenSSL, APR, APR-util, httpd) with their own autotools build systems.
      Increase to speed up the initial build on machines with many cores.

      $ cmake -B build -DDEPENDENCIES_PARALLEL=16

  DEPENDENCIES_DIRECTORY        (default: dependencies/)
      Root directory where git submodule sources live.

  DEPENDENCIES_OUTPUT_DIRECTORY (default: same as DEPENDENCIES_DIRECTORY)
      Install prefix for vendored dependency build outputs.


  Vendored Build (VENDOR_SYSTEM=ON)
  ---------------------------------

  CMake builds each system dependency from its submodule in this order:

     1. OpenSSL  -> dependencies/openssl-dist/
     2. APR      -> dependencies/apr-dist/
     3. APR-util -> dependencies/apr-util-dist/
     4. httpd    -> dependencies/httpd-dist/

  Sentinel files (dependencies/<dep>-dist/.done) prevent redundant rebuilds.
  Build logs are written to dependencies/<dep>-dist/logs/.

  To force a rebuild of a single dependency, delete its sentinel and
  re-run cmake configure:

     $ rm dependencies/openssl-dist/.done
     $ cmake -B build

  nghttp3 and googletest are always built from submodules regardless of
  VENDOR_SYSTEM.


  System Packages Build (VENDOR_SYSTEM=OFF)
  -----------------------------------------

  The following tools must be on PATH:

     apxs or apxs2       httpd >= 2.4.x, MMN >= 20211221
     apr-1-config        APR >= 1.7.0
     apu-1-config        APR-util >= 1.6.0
     openssl             OpenSSL >= 3.5.0 (with QUIC support)

  NOTE: Distro-packaged httpd (Ubuntu, Fedora, etc.) ships with an older
  MMN and will be rejected at configure time.  You need httpd built from
  the trunk branch.

  For non-standard installation prefixes, prepend the relevant bin/
  directories to PATH before configuring:

     $ export PATH="/opt/httpd/bin:/opt/openssl/bin:$PATH"
     $ cmake -B build -DVENDOR_SYSTEM=OFF
     $ cmake --build build -j$(nproc)


  Running Tests
  -------------

     $ cmake --build build -j$(nproc) --target tests

  Or run the GTest binary directly (faster -- skips the rebuild check):

     $ ./build/bin/mod_http3_tests

  To run a single test or a pattern:

     $ ./build/bin/mod_http3_tests --gtest_filter='Dependencies.OpenSSL_VersionAtLeast3_5'
     $ ./build/bin/mod_http3_tests --gtest_filter='Dependencies.OpenSSL_*'

  Sanitizer test runs:

     $ rm -rf build
     $ cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug -DENABLE_ASAN=ON
     $ cmake --build build -j$(nproc) --target tests

     $ rm -rf build
     $ cmake -B build -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug -DENABLE_UBSAN=ON
     $ cmake --build build -j$(nproc) --target tests


  Creating a Distribution Package
  --------------------------------

     $ cmake --build build -j$(nproc) --target package

  Produces a ZIP and a TGZ archive in the build directory.


  Installing
  ----------

  After a successful build, install the module and supporting files with:

     $ cmake --install build --prefix /opt/mod_http3

  This installs:

     /opt/mod_http3/lib/mod_http3.so          Apache DSO
     /opt/mod_http3/bin/mod_http3_tests        Google Test binary
     /opt/mod_http3/share/mod_http3/docs/      CHANGES, LICENSE, NOTICE

  The --prefix flag overrides the installation root at install time without
  requiring a reconfigure.  You can use any path:

     $ cmake --install build --prefix /usr/local
     $ cmake --install build --prefix /opt/mod_http3

  After installing, load the module in httpd.conf:

     LoadModule http3_module /opt/mod_http3/lib/mod_http3.so


  Inspecting the Configuration
  ----------------------------

  To print all CMake cache variables and their current values:

     $ cmake -LH -N -B build


  Postscript
  ----------

  For issues and bug reports, see the project repository.

  For httpd runtime configuration (loading the module, VirtualHost
  directives, certificate setup), see CONFIGURATION_HTTPD.md.

  For a full reference of all build options and advanced configuration,
  see CONFIGURATION.md.
